From cd149c87812795e652370e767935c524944bf93b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:43:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] CID strategy keys: match the homepage key colour exactly

The retune had lit the resting key. On the homepage .ood-key carries no
box-shadow at rest, so the face is the bare gradient, and that is the
colour read off the homepage. An inset highlight and a violet rim had been
added here, which lifted the edges and made the plate a different colour
from the one over there. Both are gone; the resting key is now the
homepage key with nothing on it.

Hover and pressed now mirror the homepage layer for layer, same colours,
same opacities, with exactly one layer dropped from each: the wide purple
bloom (0 0 18px, 0 0 16px). That is the only layer that needs darkness
behind it. Every layer that touches the key itself is kept, so the lit key
matches too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EvRZJin2PNdFtPMRwTJCdt
---
 src/styles/cid-vivarium.css | 28 ++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/styles/cid-vivarium.css b/src/styles/cid-vivarium.css
index 2b1feff..80ff164 100644
--- a/src/styles/cid-vivarium.css
+++ b/src/styles/cid-vivarium.css
@@ -892,22 +892,30 @@
    physical key pressed into a light surface. The key faces, the gradients
    and the Bright Silver legend are untouched, so the two pages still show
    the same object. */
-.cid-scope .cid-strategy-keys .ood-key {
-  box-shadow:
-    inset 0 1px 0 rgba(232,236,244,.22),
-    0 0 0 1px rgba(75,0,182,.20);
-}
+/* The resting key gets NOTHING added. On the homepage .ood-key carries no
+   box-shadow at rest: the face is the bare gradient and that is the colour
+   Greg reads off the homepage. An inset highlight or a rim here would light
+   the edges and lift the whole plate, so the key would no longer be the
+   same colour it is over there. Only the cast shadow (set per key in
+   CID.tsx) and the two interactive states below adapt to the pale ground. */
+/* Hover and pressed mirror the homepage layer for layer, same colours and
+   same opacities, with ONE layer removed from each: the wide purple bloom
+   (0 0 18px and 0 0 16px). That layer is the only one that needs darkness
+   behind it to work. Everything that touches the key itself, the lavender
+   inset, the white pressed highlight, the violet rim, is kept exactly, so
+   the lit key is the same colour here as on the homepage. */
 .cid-scope .cid-strategy-keys .ood-key:hover {
   box-shadow:
-    inset 0 1px 0 rgba(232,236,244,.30),
-    0 0 0 1px rgba(75,0,182,.46),
-    0 6px 14px -8px rgba(26,22,70,.44);
+    inset 0 1px 1px rgba(190,150,250,.42),
+    0 0 0 1px rgba(75,0,182,.42),
+    0 8px 18px -6px rgba(26,22,70,.34);
   transform: translateY(1px);
 }
 .cid-scope .cid-strategy-keys .ood-key.is-on {
   box-shadow:
-    inset 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(6,2,28,.55),
-    0 0 0 2px rgba(91,4,222,.72);
+    inset 0 2px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.30),
+    0 0 0 1px rgba(91,4,222,.72),
+    0 6px 16px -6px rgba(75,0,182,.42);
   transform: translateY(2px);
 }
 /* The lit lift on the homepage is a purple drop-shadow bloom. On light it
